# Cursor Rules for Agentic-Helper

- Rule 0 (Mandatory Parallel Multi-Tab Workers): NEVER solve sequentially one-by-one in a single tab!
  * If Specialization (`/specializations/<slug>`): Open EACH child course in its own browser tab simultaneously and complete all child courses concurrently in parallel!
  * If Single Course (`/learn/<slug>`): Open different module assignments in separate browser tabs simultaneously (Week 1, Week 2, Week 3, Week 4 Quizzes) and solve all modules concurrently in parallel!
  * Universal execution: `quiz_pilot.tab_scheduler.smart_multiworker_sync(max_concurrency=4)` or MCP tool `smart_multiworker()`.
- Rule 1 (Zero-Scratch Files): NEVER write one-off course scripts (e.g. solve_*.py, check.py) to disk. All quiz solving must run in-memory via CourseraAdapter, FastAttemptManager, or MCP tools.
- Rule 2 (Windows Browser Launcher): Use `ensure_browser(url=course_url, port=9222)`. It automatically launches Edge/Chrome and navigates to the target URL even if the browser is already running on port 9222.
- Rule 3 (Mandatory quiz_analysis.md Failure Memory & Option Elimination):
  * When an attempt scores < 100%, immediately create/update `quiz_analysis.md` via `FastAttemptManager().record_attempt(...)` or MCP `record_quiz_analysis`.
  * Lock verified correct answers as `LOCKED_CORRECT` with their exact option text.
  * Eliminate failed options as `ELIMINATED`.
  * On retry, inspect `quiz_analysis.md` via `FastAttemptManager().get_retry_answers(...)`: match by text (resilient to LMS option shuffling), lock verified choices, focus compute strictly on wrong questions, and NEVER pick a previously failed option again!
- Rule 4 (Screenshots & Cleanup): All screenshots in `.assessment_cache/screenshots/`. Run `FastAttemptManager().purge_all()` upon passing or course completion.
- Rule 5 (Direct API First with Safe DOM Fallback): Attempt direct REST API submission with grade polling and memory recording first; cleanly fall through to DOM adapter on failure or HTTP 400.
- Rule 6 (Unified Async & Tab Connection Pool): Await async tab finders (`find_assessment_page`), and utilize the WebSocket server connection pool (`active_websockets`) so multiple tabs stay connected.
- Rule 7 (100% Answer Guarantee): Never leave questions unanswered. Instant sub-millisecond failsafe check selects candidates across all inputs.
- Rule 8 (Zero Websearch): Never search web for CS/programming/cloud questions. Built-in algorithms solve locally. Search ONLY for dynamic latest news questions.
- Rule 9 (Always Speak Caveman): Terse, smart, compressed communication (~65% token savings). Drop filler/pleasantries. Accurate technical substance only.
- Rule 10 (Peer-Graded Two-Step Protocol):
  * Step 1: Always submit your own assignment first on `/submit` (title, report PDF via Uppy, video URL, honor code checkbox, submit + modal dialog confirmation). Peer reviews are locked until submitted!
  * Step 2: Only after submission is confirmed, navigate to `/give-feedback` / `/review-next` and grade 3-4 peers at MAX value: run the peer-review solver, whose one-shot rubric sweep selects the highest-points option for every criterion (never hand-click options one by one - slow). Add brief positive feedback!

## Tab Ownership Rule (multi-tab / multi-course runs)
One worker = one tab. Act ONLY on your assigned tab (identified by its URL / tab_id). Never navigate, click, fill, or submit in another worker's tab, and never fall back to "the first tab". If your assigned tab is missing or shows a different course, STOP and report it - do not adopt another tab.
